## PR Review Best Practices

### Security Checks
- **MUST** fail builds for high/critical security vulnerabilities
- Security scans should NOT use `continue-on-error: true` for blocking issues
- npm audit should fail for `--audit-level=high` or `--audit-level=critical`
- Secret scanning (TruffleHog) should block merges when secrets are detected

### Test Coverage Requirements
- **MANDATORY**: 80% minimum coverage threshold (branches, functions, lines, statements)
- Coverage thresholds MUST be enforced in CI/CD - builds will fail if not met
- Jest configuration should explicitly fail if thresholds aren't met
- CI workflow should verify coverage file generation AND threshold compliance

### Test Quality Standards
- Tests MUST include error handling scenarios (not just happy paths)
- Edge cases MUST be tested (null/undefined props, API failures, etc.)
- E2E tests MUST cover critical user flows (authentication, form submissions, error handling)
- Test mocks MUST cover both success and error scenarios

### CI/CD Workflow Best Practices
- PR summary jobs should have explicit dependencies (not all jobs)
- Use `needs: [lint, type-check, test, build]` for core checks
- Optional jobs (like E2E) should not block PR summary
- All jobs MUST have timeouts to prevent infinite hangs
- Artifact uploads should use `if: always()` to capture failures

### Code Review Checklist
When reviewing PRs, ensure:
- [ ] Security checks are blocking (not just warnings)
- [ ] Coverage thresholds are explicitly verified
- [ ] Error handling is tested
- [ ] Edge cases are covered
- [ ] E2E tests exist for critical flows
- [ ] CI workflow dependencies are explicit
- [ ] All jobs have appropriate timeouts

